ingenic: make the plugin load, and the ISP knobs work, on T41

Four problems, all on T41 and none visible on t31.

The plugin did not load at all. T41's libimp exports no GetContrast, no
GetSensorFPS and neither flip call, and musl resolves a shared object's
symbols when it is loaded rather than when they are first called - so a
single missing symbol makes dlopen() fail and every command in the plugin
goes with it, including the ones whose symbols were present. Declaring
them weak makes an absent symbol resolve to NULL instead, so the loss is
confined to the one command that needs it. Each call site checks.

blackwhite did not work. IMP_ISP_Tuning_SetISPRunningMode is exported on
T41 but faults inside the library, so keeping the same route could not
repair it. The ISP driver carries the same day/night switch as a module
parameter, so use that where it exists and fall through to the library
call where it does not - which is every other SoC, so nothing there
changes. The same applies to brightness and contrast, which is why the
lookup is written once and shared, and the module directory is found
rather than assumed because the driver is named after its SoC.

This matters beyond the plugin: majestic has no ingenic implementation of
the grey conversion - it logs "Not implemented for platform ingenic" - so
on these parts this command is the only thing that makes the picture
actually turn grey.

Only two of the streamer's four image knobs were covered. saturation,
sharpness and hue are added by the same route, so a live preview has no
sliders that silently do nothing. Hue has no library call to fall back to
on T41, where libimp exports none, so there the parameter is the only way.

And rotation reported itself unsupported. On T41 orientation belongs to
the sensor, whose driver carries it as a module parameter and now applies
it on write, so it can be set on a running stream. The sensor module is
named after the sensor and the SoC, so it too is found rather than
assumed, and the library calls remain the fallback everywhere else.

--- a/ingenic/custom.c
+++ b/ingenic/custom.c
